// Real water (TODO 37): one shared water system for every water surface on the island (the lake,
// the garden pond, the fountain, the wells, the trough, the wishing well, the falls and the river,
// and the cave beach of TODO 35), the same look on every tier:
//   - a moving surface: three scrolled layers of one shared wave tile, ripples from whoever wades
//     in or paddles about, waves lapping on a beach;
//   - reflections: the theme's own sky (the sky dome's very colours), the sun or moon glinting, the
//     banks low down, stars at night; on high/ultra a mirror picture of the island (one plane, half
//     size) for the lake and the pond;
//   - see-through shallows: the bed under the water, bent by the waves (refraction), with caustics
//     dancing on it in the sun, the colour deepening with depth (light absorbed per colour);
//   - a soft foam line along the shore and an edge that fades into it; at night the foam and little
//     sparks in the water glow, on snowy themes the edges freeze over.
// Phones draw it in one pass with no extra pictures: depth, shore and foam come from a per-vertex
// shore distance (prepared once when the mesh is bound), not from a depth picture.
//
