// ---- phones: what is drawn smaller than a few pixels is not drawn (TODO 1: the phone frame is mostly draw calls,
// ~500 a frame against 200, and a hundred of them are trims, posts, pots, glows and signs across the island a few
// pixels big). Every half second each such piece is measured against the view: one whose bounding sphere is under
// TINY of the screen's half-height (about 2.5 px of an 844 px phone) leaves the drawn layer, and comes back past
// 1.4 x that, so it never flickers on the line; at that size its coming and going is under a pixel's change.
// Layer 0 only: the piece itself, its visibility and its material are never touched.
const TINY_PHONE = 0.006;
const TINY_PC = 0.003; // (computers: under about a pixel across, the willow's view drew ~100 such pieces)
