// Everything about the house is DATA: the surfaces (every material slot: its kind and colour), the rooms and their
// floors, every wall with its doors and windows, the roof, the porch, the balcony, the garden, and every placed piece
// with its own colours. home.js builds the house from this; the editor (part 2) edits it and saves it for both of us.
//
// Frame: the house's own (the "wardrobe" place's group: +z faces the willow, where the path comes in), metres.
// The Blender kit (assets/blender/buildings/home/_build_home.py) carries every piece as one mesh per material slot,
// INST_bld_home_<file>_<piece>_s_<slot> (tdd_role "<piece>__<slot>"): a slot's mesh is drawn in that slot's material (its kind's surface detail in
// its colour; "fixed" keeps the modelled colours).

